From: MOSS Windows lane <moss@example.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] install --network-open: the network, but not the cloud metadata address

---

Upstream: anthropics/sandbox-runtime, tag v0.0.81 (c40cf14), after 0001.
Reason: MOSS runs a command the person approved to leave the sandbox as
a pool account of its own, with every other control of the sandbox, and
the spec gives that command the network. The filter set keyed to the
account's user SID blocks every connection; this adds an install mode in
which that user-keyed BLOCK matches only the cloud metadata address
(169.254.169.254 and fd00:ec2::254), so the account reaches the network
and still never the metadata service.

Files: src/wfp.rs, src/cli.rs.

What changes, and nothing else: `install --network-open` installs the
`block-metadata` filter (user SID AND remote address) at each ALE connect
layer in place of `block-user`; `status` reads either as installed. Without
the flag every install is as before.

